From f0401ea52f540b854e264f8b005b27b167ba6188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 08:47:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: Route Generate mode through PureSoft TEE

Add an internal KEYSTORE selector for the PureSoft KeyMint TEE persona
used by TEE Soft Emu Generate mode.

Keep generated key blobs associated with the SOFTWARE routing UUID
while reporting TRUSTED_ENVIRONMENT through KeyMint characteristics
and KeyInfo. This prevents the emulated device from replacing or
conflicting with the genuine TEE device.

Track the reported security level separately from the routing UUID and
preserve leaves signed by a software-generated ATTEST_KEY so their
certificate chains remain intact.

The regular SOFTWARE compatibility device remains unchanged, and TEE
Soft Emu disabled, Patch, and Auto hardware paths continue to use their
existing devices.

Change-Id: I264a7163bb5225e0af191de648873fc37d9e42f7
---
